KG42.register("clusters-a8ec2488bf82f79f995f6b04",{"id":"26-battery_flexibility::v142-d-CL003","paper":"26-battery_flexibility","label":"Pool Hub community trading and shared battery power withdrawal permission","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Pool Hub community trading and shared battery power withdrawal permission","market_meaning":"Under the shared battery design, consumers and prosumers can trade local electricity, and consumers can also obtain shared battery discharge; trading applies the dynamic price referenced by that design and prohibits grid feeding, and the related trading and power withdrawal have payment consequences. This cluster expresses the scope of permissions and obligations and does not claim to provide a complete scheduling or transaction-by-transaction settlement algorithm.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","pricing","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"All references belong to the M02 shared battery design. The shared R012 explains price applicability, and the shared R014 explains payment consequences; their price calculation and scheduling interfaces are primarily attributed to CL004. The source mentions the same Flexi User dynamic tariff, which does not mean that private battery operating conditions are introduced.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Form permission rules according to which electricity participants can trade or obtain, which community boundary applies, and what payment consequences follow; this qualitative rule can be expressed independently of central battery optimization. Storage price calculation and operational allocation are handled in CL004, and the shared chains are not counted as separate rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the execution scope of Pool Hub local trading, price applicability, and the prohibition on grid feeding."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Simultaneously defines the permission for consumers to participate in trading and to obtain shared battery discharge."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements the prosumers' trading permission in the same design."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Clarifies the local P2P electricity product permission without transferring the product mathematics of another mechanism."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References price applicability and price relations as the price context of the permission; the price rule is primarily attributed to CL004."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References the payment consequences of trading and battery power withdrawal; the compensation, price, and scheduling interfaces are primarily attributed to CL004."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CO009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g02-e02"],"rationale":"The consumer permission of the shared battery design concretizes the participant scope listed in the execution chain, and no additional participation decision variable is needed."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CO010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g02-e02"],"rationale":"The prosumer trading permission and the applicability of the same dynamic price jointly define the Pool Hub trading scope, and no new pricing dependency edge is generated on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CO011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g03-E08"],"rationale":"The product permission, together with trading entities and the no-grid-feed boundary, describes the same intra-community local trading and is not expanded to cross-community or grid trading."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CO012","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-T002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E06"],"rationale":"The Pool Hub source explicitly applies this dynamic tariff to P2P trading, supporting the connection between the price rule and the execution application; R009 has no parameter object, and no new parameter is created for it."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CO013","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The same-mechanism source states that P2P trading generates transaction costs and seller revenue, connecting trading permission and payment consequences, without supplying transaction amounts."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CO014","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g02-e17"],"rationale":"The permission for consumers to obtain shared battery discharge is complementary to the obligation to pay the discharge price for power withdrawal; the qualitative slightly higher tariff is not interpreted as an additional numerical markup."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM011","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R012::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R012::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E06"],"rationale":"The same M02 local pricing function appears in both the price definition and the trading application; unified display does not change the roles in the original chains."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM012","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R014::V::execution.energy_trade"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"Both reference Pool Hub community P2P trading; the original edges and obligation descriptions of the payment chain continue to be retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Shared battery access permission is currently attached to the consumer participation node; the storage operation and access proposal have not yet been approved, and the permission chain should not be regarded as having added a storage asset object.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p01","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually check the existing expression of access permission and the related proposal; retain the current participation node binding before approval."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"upstream_missing","description":"This cluster completes a qualitative permission and payment trigger scope. R009/R013 do not deliver definitions of trading volume or product source tracking, and R014 does not deliver transaction-by-transaction P2P revenue and expenditure amounts; therefore this cluster cannot be treated as a complete trading execution algorithm.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Retain the current qualitative scope; if it is extended into quantity execution or settlement rules, have B/C supplement the corresponding M02 objects and source constraints, and do not directly borrow M01 flow objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"unverified_source","description":"assembled only indicates that the listed permissions and obligations form a candidate with a defined scope; all supporting evidence remains unverified and has not passed independent source or scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012","v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manual inspection should check each chain and referenced paragraph, especially the participant scope, price references, and the no-grid-feed condition."}]},"rule_refs":["26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R009","26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R010","26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R011","26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R013","26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R012","26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R014"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-7f5e3dcddfa1014c","COMP-9ead8747bdf6fc35","COMP-c20e8384baea16b3","COMP-dfd0de19f78ef557","KG40-a4d1852d45e298e3","KG40-f19328f0aeb3d626"]});
